  "verbalization": "Pandaroside G appears to have a consistent relationship with Protein kinase C eta through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Pandaroside G targets Jurkat cells, which are then affected by Oleodaphnone and Cyclopent-2-Enone, and finally by Lythrine, all of which have a known target of Protein kinase C eta. These findings indicate a potential mechanism where Pandaroside G may influence the activity of Protein kinase C eta through a series of intermediate targets. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong, though indirect, relationship, likely mediated by the downstream targets. The mechanism is supported by the presence of a well-documented target in each intermediate step, reinforcing the possibility that Pandaroside G may modulate Protein kinase C eta through a complex network of interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering multiple layers of molecular interaction in understanding the biological effects of Pandaroside G.",
